AB  - Incorporating cutting-edge digital technologies such as Digital Twins (DTs) and transformer architectures offers significant opportunities for overcoming power sector key challenges, ensuring the power system's stability and reliability, and offering decision support to enhance stakeholders' participation in demand-side management (DSM) efforts, thereby bridging the “knowledge-action gap.” The aim of this chapter is to present generative artificial intelligence (AI) and large language models as a viable tool for streamlining predictive DT modeling and decision support in smart grids. The key findings of experiments show that the proposed physics-informed transformer architecture (PITA) based DT model demonstrated exceptional performance compared to the baseline model with up to 94.16% reduction in mean squared error (MSE) loss, alongside 69% improvement in consumer engagements with DSM schemes using a transformer-based chatbot.
