AB  - Business process management relies on precise, standardized process models, but creating them manually is time-consuming, error-prone, and often hampered by incomplete or inconsistent data. To address these challenges, this article presents a knowledge-driven multi-agent approach for automated business process modeling based on textual descriptions. This approach explores a solution that combines algorithmic model generation with the injection of knowledge enriched by research and iterative multi-agent reasoning. This approach has been applied in a business context and a prototype has been implemented to demonstrate its feasibility. The initial results are promising and open up several interesting areas of research.
